# =====================================================================
# CODEOWNERS for rustgate
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file routes review requests automatically when a PR touches the
# matching paths. GitHub adds every listed owner as a requested reviewer
# the moment the PR is opened or the diff changes to include a matching
# file.
#
# Layout: BROAD-TO-NARROW. CODEOWNERS uses a *last-match-wins* rule
# (https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners),
# so the catch-all goes FIRST and the path-specific overrides come AFTER.
# A PR that touches `crates/rustgate-authz/src/engine.rs` matches both
# the global `*` rule and the authz block; the authz block, being
# further down, is the one that takes effect.
#
# Sections, in order:
#   1. Catch-all default owner.
#   2. Whole-crate ownership for protocol / transport / federation /
#      server / integration crates (broad).
#   3. Build / supply-chain & CI surface (root-level config + workflows).
#   4. Documentation governance (CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY,
#      LICENSE, ADR collection).
#   5. Security-critical files within the broader crates (narrowest).
#
# This is currently a single-maintainer repo, so every rule routes to
# `@rchiofalo`. The structure exists to make the security-critical
# surface area explicit and to make a multi-reviewer expansion a
# one-line edit per row (swap `@rchiofalo` for `@<security-team>` on
# the relevant rows).
#
# Syntax reminders:
#   - Patterns are gitignore-style. Trailing `/` matches a directory.
#   - `*` matches everything; later, more specific patterns win.
#   - Owners must be valid GitHub usernames or team handles.
# =====================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
